L1TEX Sector Hit RateÃCache hit rates. A low rate means accesses are paying L2/DRAM latency. Atomics always miss in L1 and are not shown.
Low Total Hit Rate: improve coalescing (warp-stride patterns) or tile data to fit in L1.
Compare Total vs Tagged Hit Rate â€” if tagged is significantly higher, shared/uncached traffic is diluting the total."‰
+Compute_Triage.l1tex__t_sector_hit_rate.pctL1TEX Total Hit RateJgb10x_Compute_Triage_samplingz¤Compute_Triage.l1tex__t_sector_hit_rate = RatioMetric(l1tex__t_sectors_lookup_hit, RollupOp.avg, l1tex__t_sectors, RollupOp.avg, 1.0, '# of sector hits per sector')*ó
L1TEX ThroughputìFind the L1TEX throughput limiter among its internal stages. The L1 has two parallel pipelines: LSU (local, global, surface, shared, shuffle) and TC (texture reads, surface reads/atomics).
If LSU Data-Stage or TC Data-Stage is the peak, the pipeline is address/data-processing limited â€” drill into the per-space rows below to find the dominant memory type.
If L1-to-XBAR Requests is high, L1 misses are generating heavy off-chip traffic â€” check L1TEX Sector Hit Rate for cache efficiency."€
