Launch & Dispatch␀"ž
Warps LaunchedœTrack the rate at which new warps are placed onto SMs. Drops or gaps indicate stalls in the dispatch pipeline or periods where no new work is available. Cross-reference with Blocks Launched and engine activity to distinguish supply-side (dispatch) from demand-side (occupancy) limits."m
7pmsampling:tpc__warps_launched_shader_cs.sum.per_secondTotal Warps LaunchedJgr10x_TriageCompute_sampling"ê
Warps ActiveÎThe live count of warps occupying SM slots. If Average Warps Active per SM is low (under ~4), the GPU is severely underfilled â€” increase the grid size or block count. If warp count is moderate but SM throughput is still low, the bottleneck is likely warp stalls, not occupancy â€” see SM Occupancy & Stalls for stall classification."‹
Epmsampling:tpc__warps_active_shader_cs_realtime.avg.per_cycle_elapsedAverage Warps Active per SMJgr10x_TriageCompute_samplingi␀␀␀␀␀␀à?"y
Epmsampling:tpc__warps_active_shader_cs_realtime.sum.per_cycle_elapsedTotal Warps ActiveJgr10x_TriageCompute_sampling"Ô
Blocks LaunchedƒTrack the rate at which thread blocks (CTAs) are launched onto SMs. Drops or pauses reveal dispatch-pipeline stalls. If block launch rate is steady but occupancy is low, the blocks themselves may be resource-heavy â€” check Per-CTA Resource Usage for register or shared-memory pressure.
Compare Total Blocks Launched with Work Distributor CTAs Granted. If granted >> launched, the work distributor is pushing work faster than SMs can accept â€” resource exhaustion (registers, shared memory) is throttling launches."Á
