DTriageCompute.lts__average_t_sector_hit_rate_srcunit_ce_realtime.pctL2 Hit Rate from CEJgr10x_TriageCompute_samplingzœTriageCompute.lts__t_sectors_srcunit_ce_lookup_hit_realtime = CounterMetric(lts__t_sectors_srcunit_ce_realtime - lts__t_sectors_srcunit_ce_lookup_miss_realtime, '# of LTS sectors from unit CE that hit') TriageCompute.lts__t_sectors_srcunit_ce_lookup_hit_realtime:SetSustainedRate(1.0)z‰TriageCompute.lts__average_t_sector_hit_rate_srcunit_ce_realtime = RatioMetric(TriageCompute.lts__t_sectors_srcunit_ce_lookup_hit_realtime, RollupOp.sum, lts__t_sectors_srcunit_ce_realtime, RollupOp.sum, 1.0, 'proportion of L2 sector lookups from unit CE that hit')*ƒ	
L2 Throughput„Find the L2 cache throughput limiter among its internal stages. The L2 serves all VidMem (device memory) aperture accesses between the crossbar and DRAM.
If L2 Sectors is the peak, raw request volume is the limiter â€” check L2 Bandwidth per Source Unit to identify the dominant source.
If XBAR-to-L2 or L2-to-XBAR is the peak, the crossbar interconnect between SMs and L2 is saturated.
If L2 Atomic Stage is high, atomic operations are consuming significant L2 bandwidth â€” consider warp-level reductions to reduce atomic traffic.
If L2 CBC Requests is significant, lossless compression is active â€” check CBC Hit Rate to assess its benefit."t
