Per-CTA Resource UsageÖCompare per-CTA resource consumption against hardware limits to identify the occupancy bottleneck. If Avg SMEM/CTA is close to SMEM Config, shared memory is the binding limit â€” reduce per-block shared allocation or use dynamic sizing. Cross-reference with SM Register Occupancy and SM Block Occupancy to confirm which resource limits first."¬
bTriageCompute.tpc__average_bytes_mem_untagged_data_shared_allocated_compute_per_cta_realtime.ratioAvg SMEM/CTAJgb20x_TriageCompute_samplingz™TriageCompute.tpc__average_bytes_mem_untagged_data_shared_allocated_compute_per_cta_realtime = RatioMetric(tpc__l1tex_sram_bytes_mem_untagged_data_shared_allocated_compute_realtime, RollupOp.avg, tpc__ctas_active_realtime, RollupOp.avg, 100*2*1024, 'average shared memory per CTA')"å
 Warp Stall Reasons (All Samples)”Sampled distribution of reasons warps could not issue. The tallest stall category is the dominant bottleneck.
Long Scoreboard: warps waiting on memory (global/local loads) â€” improve data locality or increase occupancy to hide latency.
LG Throttle: load/store unit is full â€” reduce memory instruction density or improve coalescing.
Barrier: warps waiting at __syncthreads â€” reduce synchronization frequency or balance work across threads.
If no single stall dominates, the workload may be well-balanced or simply underutilized."`
