Constant Memory BandwidthæConstant memory requests at each cache level: DCC (uniform/scalar), IDC (indexed/vector), and GCC (shared mid-level).
High DCC Misses: the constant working set exceeds the DCC (~8KB per SM subpartition) â€” compact constants into fewer 64B-aligned regions.
High IDC Misses: non-uniform constant lookups are thrashing the IDC â€” consider moving divergent lookups to global memory with caching.
Compare with Constant Cache Hit Rates to confirm whether misses propagate all the way to L2."X
