Launch & Dispatch␀"Ÿ
Warps LaunchedœTrack the rate at which new warps are placed onto SMs. Drops or gaps indicate stalls in the dispatch pipeline or periods where no new work is available. Cross-reference with Blocks Launched and engine activity to distinguish supply-side (dispatch) from demand-side (occupancy) limits."n
7pmsampling:tpc__warps_launched_shader_cs.sum.per_secondTotal Warps LaunchedJgb10x_Compute_Triage_sampling"ì
Warps ActiveÎThe live count of warps occupying SM slots. If Average Warps Active per SM is low (under ~4), the GPU is severely underfilled â€” increase the grid size or block count. If warp count is moderate but SM throughput is still low, the bottleneck is likely warp stalls, not occupancy â€” see SM Occupancy & Stalls for stall classification."Œ
Epmsampling:tpc__warps_active_shader_cs_realtime.avg.per_cycle_elapsedAverage Warps Active per SMJgb10x_Compute_Triage_samplingi␀␀␀␀␀␀à?"z
Epmsampling:tpc__warps_active_shader_cs_realtime.sum.per_cycle_elapsedTotal Warps ActiveJgb10x_Compute_Triage_sampling"–
Blocks LaunchedƒTrack the rate at which thread blocks (CTAs) are launched onto SMs. Drops or pauses reveal dispatch-pipeline stalls. If block launch rate is steady but occupancy is low, the blocks themselves may be resource-heavy â€” check Per-CTA Resource Usage for register or shared-memory pressure.
Compare Total Blocks Launched with Work Distributor CTAs Granted. If granted >> launched, the work distributor is pushing work faster than SMs can accept â€” resource exhaustion (registers, shared memory) is throttling launches."s
;pmsampling:gr__ctas_launched_realtime.sum.per_cycle_elapsedTotal Blocks LaunchedJgb10x_Compute_Triage_sampling"…
Epmsampling:gr__workids_granted_as_ctas_realtime.sum.per_cycle_elapsedWork Distributor CTAs GrantedJgb10x_Compute_Triage_sampling"‰
Blocks ActiveThe live count of CTAs occupying SM block slots. If Average Blocks Active is low relative to the hardware maximum, the workload is too small or blocks are too resource-heavy. Compare with SM Register Occupancy and Per-CTA Resource Usage to identify the limiting resource."r
:pmsampling:tpc__ctas_active_realtime.avg.per_cycle_elapsedAverage Blocks ActiveJgb10x_Compute_Triage_sampling"p
:pmsampling:tpc__ctas_active_realtime.sum.per_cycle_elapsedTotal Blocks ActiveJgb10x_Compute_Triage_sampling"¼
CGAs Launched & CompletedÆTrack Cooperative Grid Array launches and completions. CGAs coordinate multiple blocks that co-reside on the same GPC. If CGA launches are zero, the workload does not use this feature. If non-zero, compare launches with completions â€” a persistent gap hints at CGA scheduling overhead or resource contention at the GPC level."i
3pmsampling:gpc__cgas_launched.sum.per_cycle_elapsedTotal CGAs LaunchedJgb10x_Compute_Triage_sampling"k
4pmsampling:gpc__cgas_completed.sum.per_cycle_elapsedTotal CGAs CompletedJgb10x_Compute_Triage_sampling"¥
CGAs Active±The live count of active Cooperative Grid Arrays across GPCs. Low CGA residency relative to launches may indicate scheduling constraints or resource exhaustion at the GPC level."p
:pmsampling:gpc__cgas_active_realtime.avg.per_cycle_elapsedAverage CGAs ActiveJgb10x_Compute_Triage_sampling"n
:pmsampling:gpc__cgas_active_realtime.sum.per_cycle_elapsedTotal CGAs ActiveJgb10x_Compute_Triage_sampling*Ñ
Launch & Dispatch«Look for gaps, overlaps, and idle time between GPU engines.
If GR/Compute Active is low or intermittent, the GPU is starved â€” check Warps Launched for submission gaps.
If Sync and Async Compute show little overlap, the workload may benefit from concurrent kernel execution across queues.
If Copy Engine activity overlaps with compute, verify whether host-device transfers are hiding behind useful work or creating contention."‰
Rpmsampling:gr__compute_cycles_active_queue_async.avg.pct_of_peak_sustained_elapsedAsync Compute ActiveJgb10x_Compute_Triage_sampling"q
>pmsampling:gr__cycles_active.avg.pct_of_peak_sustained_elapsedGR Engine ActiveJgb10x_Compute_Triage_sampling"q
>pmsampling:fe__cycles_active.avg.pct_of_peak_sustained_elapsedFront End ActiveJgb10x_Compute_Triage_sampling"„
Lpmsampling:gpu__gr_cycles_active_cmd_ctxsw.avg.pct_of_peak_sustained_elapsedContext Switch ActiveJgb10x_Compute_Triage_sampling"’
cpmsampling:gpu__scheduler_engine_gr_queue_sync_gpfifo_cycles_idle.avg.pct_of_peak_sustained_elapsedGP FIFO IdleJgb10x_Compute_Triage_sampling¹'
SM Compute Pipelines␀"ú
	SM Active€The fraction of cycles where at least one warp is in flight. A low SM Active indicates the SM is not being utilized effectively."j
>pmsampling:sm__cycles_active.avg.pct_of_peak_sustained_elapsed	SM ActiveJgb10x_Compute_Triage_sampling"ò
Executed IPCùCompare IPC against active cycles vs elapsed cycles. A large gap between Active and Elapsed IPC means the SM spends significant time idle.
If Active IPC itself is low (well under 1.0), warps are stalling frequently â€” see Warp Stall Reasons for the dominant stall class.
If Active IPC is healthy but Elapsed IPC is low, the problem is GPU utilization, not per-warp efficiency."p
