DRAM␀"Ò
DRAM BandwidthóDRAM bandwidth split by read and write direction. DRAM is half-duplex â€” reads and writes alternate, and direction changes cost cycles.
If the read/write ratio is roughly balanced, direction-turn overhead may be significant â€” check DRAM Read-to-Write Turns.
If one direction heavily dominates, the DRAM controller can batch efficiently and direction turns are minimal.␀"b
,pmsampling:dram__sectors_read.sum.per_secondDRAM Read BandwidthJgb10x_Compute_Triage_sampling"d
