SM Compute Pipelines␀"ù
	SM Active€The fraction of cycles where at least one warp is in flight. A low SM Active indicates the SM is not being utilized effectively."i
>pmsampling:sm__cycles_active.avg.pct_of_peak_sustained_elapsed	SM ActiveJgr10x_TriageCompute_sampling"ð
Executed IPCùCompare IPC against active cycles vs elapsed cycles. A large gap between Active and Elapsed IPC means the SM spends significant time idle.
If Active IPC itself is low (well under 1.0), warps are stalling frequently â€” see Warp Stall Reasons for the dominant stall class.
If Active IPC is healthy but Elapsed IPC is low, the problem is GPU utilization, not per-warp efficiency."o
:pmsampling:sm__inst_executed_realtime.avg.per_cycle_activeExecuted IPC ActiveJgr10x_TriageCompute_sampling"q
;pmsampling:sm__inst_executed_realtime.avg.per_cycle_elapsedExecuted IPC ElapsedJgr10x_TriageCompute_sampling"Œ
Active Threads Per WarpýThe fraction of active thread lanes per warp instruction. Lower than 100% means branch divergence or partial-warp launches are wasting SIMT lanes.
If overall thread utilization is low, check whether launch block sizes are warp-aligned (multiples of 32)."ð
UTriageCompute.sm__average_thread_inst_executed_pred_on_per_inst_executed_realtime.pctPred On per ExecutedJgr10x_TriageCompute_samplingzÌTriageCompute.sm__thread_inst_executed_pred_on = CounterMetric(RerollUp(smsp__thread_inst_executed_pred_on, RollupOp.sum, HwUnit.sm)) TriageCompute.sm__thread_inst_executed_pred_on:SetSustainedRate(128.0)z“TriageCompute.sm__average_thread_inst_executed_pred_on_per_inst_executed_realtime = RatioMetric(TriageCompute.sm__thread_inst_executed_pred_on, RollupOp.avg, sm__inst_executed_realtime, RollupOp.avg, 32.0, 'average # of active predicated-on threads per instruction executed')"Ú
Average Active Threads per InstªRaw throughput of predicated-on thread-instructions at the SMSP level, shown as a percentage of peak.
This complements the ratio view above (Pred On per Executed) with an absolute throughput measure.
If this is low while Pred On per Executed is high, the SM is simply not issuing many instructions."‰
Opmsampling:smsp__thread_inst_executed_pred_on.avg.pct_of_peak_sustained_elapsedSMSP Thread Inst Pred OnJgr10x_TriageCompute_sampling"Ä
TMEM Allocation¹Tensor memory allocation. Nonzero values indicate the kernel uses tensor memory for DMMA or other tensor operations.
Compare with SM Tensor Pipe Throughput to verify tensor utilization."u
?pmsampling:sm__mem_tensor_bytes_allocated.avg.per_cycle_elapsedTMEM Bytes AllocatedJgr10x_TriageCompute_sampling"ü
SM Tensor Pipe Breakdown¤Identify which tensor instruction families are in use.
If one sub-family dominates, the workload is specialized. If both appear, check whether mixed-precision conversions add overhead. If tensor throughput is low but expected to be high, verify the compiler is generating tensor instructions."
`pmsampling:sm__pipe_tensor_subpipe_hmma_cycles_active_realtime.avg.pct_of_peak_sustained_elapsedTensor HMMA Pipe ThroughputJgr10x_TriageCompute_sampling"–
