SMEM Allocated‹Shows how much of the shared-memory partition is actually used by resident CTAs. A large Shared Unallocated region suggests the shared-memory configuration is oversized for actual usage â€” the driver-configured SMEM size may be reducible, freeing space for L1 cache.␀"–
`pmsampling:tpc__l1tex_sram_bytes_mem_untagged_data_shared_compute_realtime.avg.per_cycle_elapsedSMEM Bytes AllocatedJgr10x_TriageCompute_sampling"Â
oTriageCompute.tpc__l1tex_sram_bytes_mem_untagged_data_shared_unallocated_compute_realtime.avg.per_cycle_elapsedSMEM Bytes UnallocatedJgr10x_TriageCompute_samplingz˜TriageCompute.tpc__l1tex_sram_bytes_mem_untagged_data_shared_unallocated_compute_realtime = CounterMetric(tpc__l1tex_sram_bytes_mem_untagged_realtime - tpc__l1tex_sram_bytes_mem_untagged_data_shared_allocated_compute_realtime, 'cumulative # of shared memory bytes unallocated for compute') TriageCompute.tpc__l1tex_sram_bytes_mem_untagged_data_shared_unallocated_compute_realtime:SetSustainedRate(328*2*1024)"ä
Per-CTA Resource UsageÖCompare per-CTA resource consumption against hardware limits to identify the occupancy bottleneck. If Avg SMEM/CTA is close to SMEM Config, shared memory is the binding limit â€” reduce per-block shared allocation or use dynamic sizing. Cross-reference with SM Register Occupancy and SM Block Occupancy to confirm which resource limits first."î
ATriageCompute.tpc__average_sharedmem_bytes_per_cta_realtime.ratioAvg SMEM Bytes/CTAJgr10x_TriageCompute_samplingzöTriageCompute.tpc__average_sharedmem_bytes_per_cta_realtime = RatioMetric(tpc__l1tex_sram_bytes_mem_untagged_data_shared_allocated_compute_realtime, RollupOp.avg, tpc__ctas_active_realtime, RollupOp.avg, 671744.0, 'average shared memory per CTA')"¼
Shared Memory Allocation DetailîDetailed view of shared-memory SRAM allocation.
SMEM SRAM Lines shows how many L1TEX SRAM lines are dedicated to shared memory across resident CTAs.
Compare with L1TEX Data Occupancy to confirm shared memory is the dominant SRAM consumer."¥
jpmsampling:tpc__l1tex_sram_lines_mem_untagged_data_shared_allocated_compute_realtime.avg.per_cycle_elapsedSMEM SRAM Lines AllocatedJgr10x_TriageCompute_sampling"‰
Warp Stall ScoreboardÉBreakdown of scoreboard-related warp stalls. Long Scoreboard stalls indicate warps waiting on long-latency operations (typically global memory loads). Short Scoreboard stalls indicate warps waiting on short-latency operations (shared memory, L1 cache).
If Long Scoreboard dominates, improve global memory access patterns or increase occupancy to hide memory latency.
If Short Scoreboard dominates, reduce shared-memory bank conflicts or L1 cache contention."Ž
