SM Occupancy & StallsOnly investigate occupancy if SM Issue Throughput (in SM Compute Pipelines) is low. Occupancy is a means, not an end. The goal is hiding latency.
Fewer than 4 warps/SM is a starvation condition: launch bigger grids or increase block count.
Above ~16 warps/SM, additional occupancy rarely helps hide math-pipe latency.
If Warps Inactive (SM Active) is large, an occupancy limiter is preventing more warps from being scheduled - check the resource rows below (registers, shared memory, block count) to find which limit is binding.␀"ˆ
