L2 Bandwidth per Source Unit¹Identify which unit is driving L2 traffic. The dominant bar is the primary L2 consumer.
L1TEX dominates (typical): SM load/store misses are the primary L2 consumer â€” optimize L1 hit rates in the L1 Data Cache & LSU group.
GCC is significant: constant or instruction cache pressure is spilling to L2 â€” check Constant & Instruction Caches group.
CE is significant: host-device DMA transfers are contending for L2 bandwidth â€” check if transfers can be overlapped or reduced.
HUB is significant: system-level traffic (e.g. page table walks) is consuming L2 bandwidth.␀"p
