Interconnect␀"ä
PCIe Bandwidth‹PCIe bandwidth by direction (RX = GPU reads from host, TX = GPU writes to host). PCIe is full-duplex, so both directions can run simultaneously at full rate.
If RX dominates: the GPU is reading data from the host â€” consider pre-staging this data into device memory.
If TX dominates: the GPU is writing results back to the host â€” consider batching or reducing write-back frequency.
If both are active during kernel execution, mapped/pinned memory may be in use â€” migrate hot buffers to device memory for lower latency."_
