/SysL2 Atomic Sectors per Operation (from L1TEX)­Total atomic sector volume arriving at SysL2 from the SM. Compare with SysL2 Atomic Hit in the row above to compute the atomic miss rate. Cross-aperture atomics pay PCIe/NVLink round-trip latency and should be minimized â€” use device-local reductions and only write the final result to system memory."è
KTriageCompute.syslts__t_sectors_srcunit_tex_op_atom_realtime.sum.per_second!SysL2 Atomic Sectors (from L1TEX)Jgb20x_TriageCompute_samplingz×TriageCompute.syslts__t_sectors_srcunit_tex_op_atom_realtime = CounterMetric(syslts__t_sectors_srcunit_tex_realtime - syslts__t_sectors_srcunit_tex_op_read_realtime - syslts__t_sectors_srcunit_tex_op_write_realtime)*Â
SysL2 ThroughputèFind the SysL2 throughput limiter. The SysL2 cache serves system-memory and peer-memory aperture accesses â€” traffic that crosses PCIe or NVLink instead of going to local DRAM.
If SysL2 throughput is unexpectedly high, data may be allocated in the wrong memory aperture â€” move hot buffers to device memory (cudaMalloc) and copy data explicitly.
If both SysL2 and L2 (SysMem Path) show traffic, cross-reference with PCIe Bandwidth in the Interconnect group to check for PCIe saturation."v
