SM Compute Pipelines—Identify which SM compute pipe is the throughput limiter. The highest bar is the bottleneck pipe.
If one pipe (FMA, ALU Heavy, Tensor, XU) is clearly dominant, focus optimization on reducing its workload â€” see the instruction-mix and thread-divergence rows below.
If SM Issue Throughput is high but no single pipe dominates, the workload has a balanced instruction mix â€” algorithmic restructuring or library offload may be needed.
If all pipes are low, the SM is not compute-bound â€” return to Top-Level Throughput to re-classify."|
