Shared Memory␀"‹
Shared Memory Bandwidth·Effective vs wasted shared-memory bandwidth. Imputed Bandwidth Overhead is bandwidth lost to inactive thread lanes and bank conflicts.
If Overhead is large relative to useful Read/Atom bandwidth, the access pattern is inefficient â€” remap thread-to-bank mapping to reduce conflicts, or ensure warps are fully active.
High Atom bandwidth suggests frequent shared-memory atomics â€” consider warp-level shuffle reductions as an alternative.␀"z
@pmsampling:sm__bytes_mem_shared_cmd_read_realtime.sum.per_secondSM Shared Read BandwidthJgb20y_TriageCompute_sampling"z
@pmsampling:sm__bytes_mem_shared_cmd_atom_realtime.sum.per_secondSM Shared Atom BandwidthJgb20y_TriageCompute_sampling"ø
QTriageCompute.l1tex__data_bytes_mem_shared_cmd_read_value_overhead.sum.per_secondShared Read OverheadJgb20y_TriageCompute_samplingzwTriageCompute.l1tex_data_bytes_per_wavefronts = ConversionFactorMetric(128.0, DimUnit.bytes / DimUnit.l1tex_wavefronts)zõTriageCompute.l1tex__data_bytes_mem_shared_cmd_read_value_overhead = CounterMetric(FMax(l1tex__data_pipe_lsu_wavefronts_mem_shared_op_ld * TriageCompute.l1tex_data_bytes_per_wavefronts - sm__bytes_mem_shared_cmd_read_realtime, ConstantCounterMetric(HwUnit.tpc, 0.0, DimUnit.bytes))) TriageCompute.l1tex__data_bytes_mem_shared_cmd_read_value_overhead:SetSustainedRate(128.0)"½
QTriageCompute.l1tex__data_bytes_mem_shared_cmd_atom_value_overhead.sum.per_secondShared Atom OverheadJgb20y_TriageCompute_samplingzwTriageCompute.l1tex_data_bytes_per_wavefronts = ConversionFactorMetric(128.0, DimUnit.bytes / DimUnit.l1tex_wavefronts)zºTriageCompute.l1tex__data_bytes_mem_shared_cmd_atom_value_overhead = CounterMetric(l1tex__data_pipe_lsu_wavefronts_mem_shared_op_atom * TriageCompute.l1tex_data_bytes_per_wavefronts - sm__bytes_mem_shared_cmd_atom_realtime) TriageCompute.l1tex__data_bytes_mem_shared_cmd_atom_value_overhead:SetSustainedRate(128.0)"€
Jpmsampling:l1tex__data_pipe_lsu_wavefronts_mem_shared_op_st.sum.per_secondShared ST WavefrontsJgb20y_TriageCompute_sampling"‡
Shared Memory Imputed BandwidthÉWavefront-level breakdown of shared-memory accesses by operation. Each wavefront is one 128-byte data-array access regardless of how many threads participate.
If LD + ST + Atom wavefronts are much higher than expected from SM-level shared instructions, bank conflicts are generating replay wavefronts â€” check Shared Bank Conflict Ratios for per-op conflict rates.
High LDGSTS wavefronts indicate asynchronous copy (cp.async) staging through shared memory.␀"€
Jpmsampling:l1tex__data_pipe_lsu_wavefronts_mem_shared_op_ld.sum.per_secondShared LD WavefrontsJgb20y_TriageCompute_sampling"€
