Active Threads Per WarpýThe fraction of active thread lanes per warp instruction. Lower than 100% means branch divergence or partial-warp launches are wasting SIMT lanes.
If overall thread utilization is low, check whether launch block sizes are warp-aligned (multiples of 32)."ð
UTriageCompute.sm__average_thread_inst_executed_pred_on_per_inst_executed_realtime.pctPred On per ExecutedJgr10x_TriageCompute_samplingzÌTriageCompute.sm__thread_inst_executed_pred_on = CounterMetric(RerollUp(smsp__thread_inst_executed_pred_on, RollupOp.sum, HwUnit.sm)) TriageCompute.sm__thread_inst_executed_pred_on:SetSustainedRate(128.0)z“TriageCompute.sm__average_thread_inst_executed_pred_on_per_inst_executed_realtime = RatioMetric(TriageCompute.sm__thread_inst_executed_pred_on, RollupOp.avg, sm__inst_executed_realtime, RollupOp.avg, 32.0, 'average # of active predicated-on threads per instruction executed')"Ú
Average Active Threads per InstªRaw throughput of predicated-on thread-instructions at the SMSP level, shown as a percentage of peak.
This complements the ratio view above (Pred On per Executed) with an absolute throughput measure.
If this is low while Pred On per Executed is high, the SM is simply not issuing many instructions."‰
