SysL2 & System Memory␀"­
!System Memory Aperture Throughput‘Track system-memory traffic at each stage from SysL2 cache to PCIe. A large gap between SysL2 Request and SysL2 Miss indicates the SysL2 cache is absorbing some traffic.
If PCIe RX/TX bandwidth is near PCIe link capacity, host-device communication is a bottleneck â€” overlap transfers with compute, or reduce transfer volume.
If SysL2 Miss is high but PCIe is low, NVLink or peer paths may be active."€
