'L1TEX Tag-Stage Bandwidth per Operation‰Per-operation hit/miss breakdown across all tagged memory spaces. Use this to pinpoint exactly which access type has poor cache behavior.
High Local LD/ST Miss: register spilling is exceeding L1 capacity â€” reduce registers per thread or improve per-thread data reuse.
High Global LD Miss: scattered or strided access patterns â€” improve coalescing and consider tiling to increase cache reuse.
High Texture Miss: working set exceeds cache â€” reduce texture footprint per warp, or increase spatial locality of accesses.␀"…
