L1TEX Throughput˜Find the L1TEX throughput limiter among its internal stages. The L1 has two parallel pipelines: LSU (local, global, surface, shared, shuffle) and TEX (texture reads, surface reads/atomics).
If SRAM Array throughput is high, on-chip memory bandwidth is saturated â€” check whether shared memory or tagged cache is the dominant consumer in L1TEX Data Occupancy.
If LSU Data-Stage or TEX Data-Stage is the peak, the pipeline is address/data-processing limited â€” drill into the per-space rows below to find the dominant memory type.
If L1-to-XBAR Requests is high, L1 misses are generating heavy off-chip traffic â€” check L1TEX Sector Hit Rate for cache efficiency."†
