"L2 Sector Hit Rate per Source UnitèPer-source-unit L2 hit rates. Compare across source units to find which one has the poorest L2 cache behavior and is contributing the most to DRAM pressure.
Low L1TEX hit rate: SM data accesses are missing in L2 â€” improve data locality or reduce working set.
Low GCC hit rate: constant/instruction data is missing in L2 â€” unusual and indicates very large constant or code footprints.
Low CE hit rate: DMA traffic is not benefiting from L2 â€” this is expected for streaming transfers."z
