Warp Stall ScoreboardÉBreakdown of scoreboard-related warp stalls. Long Scoreboard stalls indicate warps waiting on long-latency operations (typically global memory loads). Short Scoreboard stalls indicate warps waiting on short-latency operations (shared memory, L1 cache).
If Long Scoreboard dominates, improve global memory access patterns or increase occupancy to hide memory latency.
If Short Scoreboard dominates, reduce shared-memory bank conflicts or L1 cache contention."
Vpmsampling:smsp__warps_issue_stalled_long_scoreboard.avg.pct_of_peak_sustained_elapsedLong Scoreboard StallsJgb10x_Compute_Triage_sampling"‘
