L2 Hit MissÒOverall L2 cache hit vs miss throughput. If Lookup Miss is a large fraction of total, most L2 accesses pay full DRAM latency.
High miss rate + high L2 Sectors: the aggregate working set exceeds L2 capacity â€” consider tiling or blocking algorithms to improve temporal reuse.
High miss rate + low L2 Sectors: traffic is sparse but misses frequently â€” likely a scattered access pattern. Check L1TEX Tag-Stage Bandwidth per Operation for the problematic access type."Ò
L2 Sector Hit Rate (Total)ÎAggregate L2 cache hit rate. For latency-limited workloads, this is a key diagnostic: low hit rates mean memory accesses pay full DRAM latency, directly increasing warp stall cycles. If below ~80%, check L2 Bandwidth per Source Unit and L2 Sector Hit Rate per Source Unit to identify which traffic source has the worst cache behavior."c
