GCC Hit RatesŸPer-type GCC hit rates. Low rates in any category indicate that cache type is thrashing and generating L2 traffic.
Low Instruction Hit Rate: kernel code footprint exceeds GCC capacity â€” reduce unrolling, use force-no-inline, or split large kernels.
Low Constant Hit Rate: constant address diversity exceeds cache â€” compact data into 64B/256B-aligned cache-friendly regions and reduce indexed constant loads.
Low TSHeader Hit Rate: too many unique texture/sampler descriptors are in use â€” reduce descriptor count or batch similar lookups."}
