SysL2 Hit Miss per Source Unit¿Per-source-unit hit and miss sector counts at SysL2. Pair with SysL2 Bandwidth per Source Unit to see both total traffic and cache effectiveness in absolute terms.
If L1TEX misses dominate, SM data accesses are crossing to system memory uncached â€” move the backing allocation to device DRAM.
If GCC or HUB misses appear, constant or system traffic is reaching the SysL2 â€” investigate whether these accesses should target device memory instead."
