L2 Sector Hit Rates from L1TEXáL2 hit rates specifically for traffic originating from the SM. Low rates here mean the data is missing both L1 and L2 â€” every such access pays full DRAM or system-memory latency.
Low Read Hit Rate: the working set exceeds L2 capacity, or access patterns are too scattered â€” reduce the active data footprint or improve temporal reuse.
Low Write Hit Rate: many writes are allocating new L2 lines â€” normal for streaming writes but costly for read-modify-write patterns.
Low Atomic Hit Rate: atomic targets are not cached â€” distribute atomic operations across more addresses, or use warp-level reductions."“
MTriageCompute.lts__average_t_sector_hit_rate_srcunit_tex_op_read_realtime.pctL2 Hit Rate from L1TEX ReadsJgb20y_TriageCompute_samplingzÑTriageCompute.lts__t_sectors_srcunit_tex_op_read_lookup_hit_realtime = CounterMetric(lts__t_sectors_srcunit_tex_op_read_realtime - lts__t_sectors_srcunit_tex_op_read_lookup_miss_realtime, '# of LTS sectors from unit L1TEX for all reads that hit') TriageCompute.lts__t_sectors_srcunit_tex_op_read_lookup_hit_realtime:SetSustainedRate(2.0)z±TriageCompute.lts__average_t_sector_hit_rate_srcunit_tex_op_read_realtime = RatioMetric(TriageCompute.lts__t_sectors_srcunit_tex_op_read_lookup_hit_realtime, RollupOp.avg, lts__t_sectors_srcunit_tex_op_read_realtime, RollupOp.avg, 1.0, 'proportion of L2 sector lookups from unit L1TEX for reads that hit')"ž
NTriageCompute.lts__average_t_sector_hit_rate_srcunit_tex_op_write_realtime.pctL2 Hit Rate from L1TEX WritesJgb20y_TriageCompute_samplingzÖTriageCompute.lts__t_sectors_srcunit_tex_op_write_lookup_hit_realtime = CounterMetric(lts__t_sectors_srcunit_tex_op_write_realtime - lts__t_sectors_srcunit_tex_op_write_lookup_miss_realtime, '# of LTS sectors from unit L1TEX for all writes that hit') TriageCompute.lts__t_sectors_srcunit_tex_op_write_lookup_hit_realtime:SetSustainedRate(1.0)zµTriageCompute.lts__average_t_sector_hit_rate_srcunit_tex_op_write_realtime = RatioMetric(TriageCompute.lts__t_sectors_srcunit_tex_op_write_lookup_hit_realtime, RollupOp.avg, lts__t_sectors_srcunit_tex_op_write_realtime, RollupOp.avg, 1.0, 'proportion of L2 sector lookups from unit L1TEX for writes that hit')"Ž	
MTriageCompute.lts__average_t_sector_hit_rate_srcunit_tex_op_atom_realtime.pctL2 Hit Rate from L1TEX AtomicsJgb20y_TriageCompute_samplingzËTriageCompute.lts__t_sectors_srcunit_tex_op_atom_realtime = CounterMetric(lts__t_sectors_srcunit_tex_realtime - lts__t_sectors_srcunit_tex_op_read_realtime - lts__t_sectors_srcunit_tex_op_write_realtime)zÞTriageCompute.lts__t_sectors_srcunit_tex_op_atom_lookup_hit_realtime = CounterMetric(TriageCompute.lts__t_sectors_srcunit_tex_op_atom_realtime - (lts__t_sectors_srcunit_tex_lookup_miss_realtime - lts__t_sectors_srcunit_tex_op_read_lookup_miss_realtime - lts__t_sectors_srcunit_tex_op_write_lookup_miss_realtime), '# of LTS sectors from unit L1TEX for all atomics or reductions that hit') TriageCompute.lts__t_sectors_srcunit_tex_op_atom_lookup_hit_realtime:SetSustainedRate(1.0)zÏTriageCompute.lts__average_t_sector_hit_rate_srcunit_tex_op_atom_realtime = RatioMetric(TriageCompute.lts__t_sectors_srcunit_tex_op_atom_lookup_hit_realtime, RollupOp.avg, TriageCompute.lts__t_sectors_srcunit_tex_op_atom_realtime, RollupOp.avg, 1.0, 'proportion of L2 sector lookups from unit L1TEX for atomics or reductions that hit')"¬
L1TEX Cache Capacity per WarpúThe effective L1 cache capacity available to each resident warp. If L1 hit rates are low and this per-warp capacity is small, too many warps are sharing the L1 cache and thrashing each others data. Reducing occupancy (fewer warps, more cache per warp) or reducing the per-warp working set can improve hit rates â€” but only if the cache improvement outweighs the occupancy loss."
;TriageCompute.tpc__l1tex_average_cache_bytes_per_warp.ratioCache Bytes per WarpJgb20y_TriageCompute_samplingzÁTriageCompute.tpc__warps_active = CounterMetric(RerollUp(smsp__warps_active, RollupOp.sum, HwUnit.tpc), 'cumulative # of warps in flight') TriageCompute.tpc__warps_active:SetSustainedRate(96.0)zÕTriageCompute.tpc__l1tex_average_cache_bytes_per_warp = RatioMetric(tpc__l1tex_sram_bytes_mem_tagged_realtime, RollupOp.avg, TriageCompute.tpc__warps_active, RollupOp.avg, 128*1024, 'average cache bytes per warp')*²
L1TEX Throughput˜Find the L1TEX throughput limiter among its internal stages. The L1 has two parallel pipelines: LSU (local, global, surface, shared, shuffle) and TEX (texture reads, surface reads/atomics).
If SRAM Array throughput is high, on-chip memory bandwidth is saturated â€” check whether shared memory or tagged cache is the dominant consumer in L1TEX Data Occupancy.
If LSU Data-Stage or TEX Data-Stage is the peak, the pipeline is address/data-processing limited â€” drill into the per-space rows below to find the dominant memory type.
If L1-to-XBAR Requests is high, L1 misses are generating heavy off-chip traffic â€” check L1TEX Sector Hit Rate for cache efficiency."†
