If Instruction Requests dominate, the kernel has a large code footprint â€” consider reducing it.
If Constant Requests dominate, the constant working set is spilling through GCC â€” compact constant data layouts.
If TSHeader Requests are significant, the kernel uses many unique texture/sampler descriptors â€” try reducing descriptor diversity.␀"x
